@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "FAQs";
}

<div class="cs-content-page">
    <h1>FAQs</h1>

    <div class="cs-faq-item">
        <h6>What is Ctrl + Save?</h6>
        <p>Ctrl + Save is a second-hand online store that gives items a second chance at life by.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cs-faq-item">
        <h6>Do you only sell pre-loved items?</h6>
        <p>Yes.</p>
    </div>

        <div class="cs-faq-item">
        <h6>How are the items priced?</h6>
        <p>The price of items are based on their current condition and market value to allow a fair and reasonable price for every target market.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cs-faq-item">
        <h6>Are prices negotiable?</h6>
        <p>No, the prices are fixed.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cs-faq-item">
        <h6>Can the items be shipped nationwide?</h6>
        <p>Yes, nationwide shipping is supported. Depending on where you live and the courier used, shipping costs may vary.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cs-faq-item">
        <h6>Can I reserve an item?</h6>
        <p>No, everything is on a "first come, first serve" basis so that there's a fair chance for everyone to get great savings.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cs-faq-item">
        <h6>How are items inspected and authenticated?</h6>
        <p>Sellers are to provide proof of ownership of the item they wish to list. Our team then cleans the items and checks that they meet the predefined standards before being sold. item goes through our in-house review team who also list the items for the buyer. Our team discusses the items, and approves the ones that pass the quality check.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cs-faq-item">
        <h6>How safe is it to buy on Ctrl + Save?</h6>
        <p>Safety is taken seriously here at Ctrl + Save. Details of the seller are verified, along with their items as they go through a check process to allow a reliable place for buyers to get great deals.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="text-center mt-4">
        <a asp-controller="Support" asp-action="Index" class="cs-btn">Back to Support Hub</a>
    </div>
</div>
